\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2011\par 11:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREEKS EYE FORMER ECB VICE PRESIDENT PAPADEMOS AS NEW PM-SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's embattled Socialists and the rival opposition party are converging on naming former European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Vice President Lucas Papademos to lead an interim government, sources said Monday, although no deal has yet been reached.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: GREEK PREMIER TO STEP DOWN AS PARTIES AGREE TO SET COALITION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's major political parties on Sunday agreed to form a national unity government that will oversee elections after putting in place a debt-slashing deal, in the hope of averting financial catastrophe and winning back the trust of the nation's European partners.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANKS' ECB OVERNIGHT DEPOSITS HIT 2011 HIGH, CLOSE TO POST-LEHMAN PEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banks' overnight deposits with the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose further Friday, hitting a new high for the year for a second consecutive day, data released by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ITALIAN GOVERNMENT BOND YIELDS HIT EURO-ERA HIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on the 10-year Italian government bond hit a euro-era high in early trade Monday, fueled by weekend comments from European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Yves Mersch that the option of not buying Italian debt had been discussed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB BUYING ITALIAN, SPANISH GOVT BONDS - TRADER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday bought Italian government bonds after yields surged sharply to their highest levels since the inception of the euro, a trader familiar with the matter said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB'S ORDONEZ WELCOMES NEW GREEK GOVERNMENT AS "GOOD FOR EUROPE" \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing council member Miguel Fernandez Ordonez welcomed Monday the latest political developments in Greece. Greece's major political parties agree to form a unity government that will oversee elections after putting in place a debt-slashing deal. The deal came about after Prime Minister George Papandreou agreed to step down.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWISS FRANC BUCKLES AFTER SWISS PRICE GROWTH REVERSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss franc fell sharply across the board Monday as traders fled the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after inflation data from the country revealed that the strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is pushing the economy towards deflationary territory, but analysts said the weak data print will not trigger more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  yet.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUND OFFICIAL SLAMS 'INDOLENCE' IN EUROPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A top official of China's $400 billion sovereign wealth fund has accused Europe of "indolence" and said any Chinese investment in the debt-laden region would be based on financial returns.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA CRITICISES U.S. AGENDA ITEMS FOR HAWAII APEC SUMMIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese officials on Monday criticised the items on the U.S.'s agenda for the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit, including proposals on environmental policy and a U.S.-led free trade initiative.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRANCE TO UNVEIL CUTS IN SPENDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The French government is finalizing an austerity package that will be unveiled Monday as it seeks to meet its deficit-reduction targets and hold on to its prized triple-A credit rating against a backdrop of slowing growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: OLD DEBTS DOG EUROPE'S BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European banks are sitting on heaps of exotic mortgage products and other risky assets that predate the financial crisis, adding to pressure on lenders that also are holding large quantities of euro-zone government debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB'S PARAMO SAYS HEDGE FUNDS MUST BE SUPERVISED - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hedge funds and other "shadow banking" entities must come under supervision from central banks such as the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , executive board member Jose Manuel Gonzalez-Paramo said in an interview Monday in El Pais newspaper.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CANADA FIN MIN: NO CONSENSUS FOR IMF TO HELP BOOST EFSF - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund is unlikely to provide money to help boost the firepower of the euro zone's rescue fund, the European Financial Stability Facility, Canadian Finance Minister Jim Flaherty said in an interview published Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB'S NOYER: EURO-ZONE COUNTRIES MUST FIX FINANCES THEMSELVES -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro-zone countries must fix their finances themselves as the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's role is not to finance countries indefinitely, ECB governing council member Christian Noyer said Sunday in an interview with weekly Le Journal du Dimanche.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU INSURANCE REGULATOR WARNS CURRENT CRISIS "WORSE THAN 2008" - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's current crisis is worse for the insurance industry than the crisis of 2008, the head of the European Union's insurance industry regulator said in an interview published Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWISS CONSUMER PRICES DECLINE IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss consumer price index fell 0.1% on the month in October, as lower prices for new and used cars outweighed higher energy and clothing costs, data released Monday showed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLDMAN SACHS O'NEILL: NEED GOOD NEWS ON ITALY THIS WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Strains in Italian government debt pose a bigger risk to the global economy than stresses in Greece, and positive news is needed urgently to help ease market concerns, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jim O'Neill\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chairman of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  (GS) Asset Management said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA FOREIGN MINISTRY OFFICIAL: SOME U.S. GOALS FOR APEC SUMMIT TOO AMBITIOUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some of the U.S.'s goals for the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation forum, or APEC Summit, are too ambitious, Wu Hailong, assistant minister of China's Ministry of Foreign Affairs, said at a press briefing Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SOFT JOB MARKET PAVES WAY FOR SECOND RATE CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Conditions in Australia's job market continued to deteriorate in October giving the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more scope to cut interest rates over coming months, a report showed Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SEOUL HANGS ON TO 2011 GROWTH TARGET, BACKS OFF CPI GOAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government on Monday held onto its 4.5% economic growth target for 2011 but acknowledged that inflation for Asia's fourth-largest economy will exceed its aim for the year, underscoring a difficult policy environment amid growing global uncertainties.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PBOC ADVISOR: GDP GROWTH MAY FALL TO 8.5% IN 2012 - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic growth may slow to 8.5% and inflation may fall to 2.8% next year, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Monday, citing a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  advisor.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA THINK TANK RESEARCHER: CPI RISE MAY FALL TO 5.5% OR LOWER IN 4Q-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's inflation may fall to 5.5% or lower in the fourth quarter as consumer price rise may be around 5.5% in October and it will continue to slow down in the following two months, the China Securities Journal reported Monday, citing a think tank researcher.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PREMIER WEN: CHINA MUST BE RESOLUTE WITH PROPERTY TIGHTENING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China must resolutely carry out its property tightening measures and the government aims for prices to return to "reasonable levels," Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said at a speech in Russia broadcast on Phoenix TV Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: TRUST FINANCING TO CHINA PROPERTY DEVELOPERS FALLS 17% IN 3Q FROM 2Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New financing provided by China's trust companies to property developers fell 17% in the third quarter from a quarter earlier, according to an industry association.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN INFLATION STILL BENIGN LEAVING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ROOM TO STAND PAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's consumer price index stayed fairly stable in October, further affirming consensus among economists that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is able to leave its policy interest rates unchanged for the near term to boost the island's export-reliant economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par INTERVIEW: STRONG SWISS FRANC TO PUSH UNEMPLOYMENT HIGHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rate of Swiss unemployment climbed for the first time in a year in October due largely to the ongoing strength of the franc, but also because of the high decgree of economic uncertainty in the rest of Europe, the country's Director of Labor Serge Gaillard said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: CHINA VANKE: CHINA UNLIKELY TO LOOSEN POLICY DESPITE EASING PROPERTY PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China isn't likely to loosen its tightening policy in the short term, even though property prices in some cities have started falling, said a senior executive from \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Vanke Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the nation's largest developer by market share.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: ASIAN RIVALS HAVE OPPOSITE, SIMILAR PROBLEM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What does a tax revolt in eastern China have in common with pre-election spending in India? Answer: Both show the limits on Beijing and New Delhi's power to tax and spend. [ 07-11-11 1008GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111107e7b7000q3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
