\par\par \b \uc2 Financial Services Top Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2011\par 22:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCIAL SERVICES TOP STORIES \par  \par BANK OF AMERICA JOB CUTS MAY REACH 40,000 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials discuss cutting about 40,000 positions during a first wave of a restructuring, people familiar with the plans tell The Wall Street Journal. Shares are down 1%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LEHMAN MANAGERS DON'T WANT FULD, OTHERS TO DRAIN INSURANCE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former leaders in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lehman Brothers\f28 \uc2 \f2  mortgage-securitization unit want to block ex-CEO Dick Fuld and other top brass from exhausting $250 million in executive-protection policies and leave more junior managers without insurance against a pending $4 billion lawsuit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WELLS FARGO WEIGHS BID FOR KBC PRIVATE BANKING UNIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. banking giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo\f28 \uc2 \f2  is considering placing a bid for the private banking business of Belgian bank \f28 \uc2 \f2 KBC Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a person familiar with the situation says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB'S STARK TO LEAVE POST BY END OF YEAR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ECB executive board member Juergen Stark will step down by end of the year, more than two years before his term was due to end, ECB says. Germany may nominate its deputy finance minister, Joerg Asmussen, to replace him, source says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH SAYS CREDIT CARD DEFAULTS UP IN AUGUST \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The credit-rating firm says credit-card defaults rose to 6.41% in August from 6.33% in July. Current charge-off levels are 35% lower than a year earlier and are now tracking close to the historical average of 6%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LAGARDE FEARS GROWTH RISKS HAVE INCREASED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Downside risks to growth across the world have increased and countries must act now, boldly and together, Christine Lagarde, managing director of the International Monetary Fund, says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GEITHNER SAYS EUROPE MUST SHOW POLITICAL WILL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasury Secretary Tim Geithner says in an interview on Bloomberg TV that European nations are under pressure to show enough political will to deal with financial crises roiling the continent, adding they have 'more work to do in that area.'\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JP MORGAN\f28 \uc2 \f2  SAYS OBAMA MOVE SHOULD AVERT U.S. RECESSION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fresh measures promised by U.S. President Barack Obama to boost the economy should steer the country clear of recession, the global head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at investment bank \f28 \uc2 \f2 JP Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SEC MOVE SIGNALS ITS FRUSTRATIONS WITH CHINA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Securities and Exchange Commission opens a new front in its battle to tighten oversight of U.S.-listed Chinese companies with its court challenge against the China unit of accounting giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SENATE VOTE HIKES US BORROWING LIMIT BY $500B \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. Senate defeats an attempt by Republicans to slow down a $500 billion increase in the federal government's borrowing limit in a vote that means the borrowing limit is immediately hiked to $15.19 trillion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH REITERATES WARNING OF BANK RISK TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RATING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings expects \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's government to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the country's banks, but warned again that this support "carries negative implications for the sovereign rating."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FANNIE, FREDDIE SAID NEAR SETTLEMENT WITH SEC \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fannie Mae\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Freddie Mac\f28 \uc2 \f2  are close to a settlement with the Securities and Exchange Commission over whether they adequately disclosed their exposure to risky subprime loans, The New York Times reports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BERNANKE SAYS FED READY TO ACT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke says the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has the tools to provide more support to the sluggish U.S. economy, but declines to say whether it's prepared to use them in less than two weeks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NASDAQ PUSHES HARDER AGAINST NYSE TIE-UP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq OMX Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  steps up its opposition to the planned merger between \f28 \uc2 \f2 NYSE Euronext\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Deutsche Boerse saying the deal would "irrevocably destroy" competition in Europe's listed-derivatives markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-09-11 1600ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110909e799000x2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
