BLEMATIC CAPITAL FLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Wednesday warned that attempts to avoid crises with capital controls may stem inflows of desirable foreign money, arguing that regulatory measures should only be used to address capital flows that can disrupt economic fundamentals.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOC'S MACKLEM SAYS G-20 FALLS SHORT IN CORRECTING IMBALANCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A top Canadian central banker said Wednesday the G-20 has fallen short in correcting global imbalances and that the spillover effects of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies are prompting other countries to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in their own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets and adopt measures to curb capital inflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA TRADE SURPLUS TO SHRINK FURTHER IN 2011 -MINISTRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus is likely to keep shrinking in 2011 and the jump in its July trade surplus was due to "chance," Chinese Commerce Ministry spokesman Shen Danyang said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA SHOULD STRENGTHEN, IMPROVE MACROECONOMIC CONTROLS - PAPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should continue to strengthen and improve macroeconomic controls, and steady its policy direction as inflationary pressures remain, the People's Daily said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: CHINA MOVES CLOSER TO ACCEPTING REBEL TAKEOVER IN LIBYA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's government appeared to move closer to accepting a rebel takeover of Libya, praising the rebel leadership group in a statement Wednesday and saying it hoped the "new regime" will help restore stability in the war-torn North African nation. (published 0502 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \p