\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Majors\b0\par\par\uc2 1,651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2011\par 01:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range   Larger Range \par USD/JPY    76.70-77.51      76.25-77.86 \par EUR/USD   1.4195-1.4402    1.4152-1.4432 \par AUD/USD   1.0062-1.0445    0.9924-1.0526 \par NZD/USD   0.8066-0.8438    0.7959-0.8465 \par GBP/USD   1.6174-1.6410    1.6120-1.6470 \par USD/CHF   0.7068-0.7325    0.7000-0.7447 \par USD/CAD   0.9740-0.9956    0.9684-1.0009 \par EUR/JPY   110.24-112.68    109.23-113.85 \par EUR/GBP   0.8755-0.8847    0.8675-0.8883 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent high and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/JPY - to range-trade. Undermined by weaker USD sentiment (ICE spot dollar index last 73.90 vs 74.84 early Tuesday) after U.S. Federal Reserve pledged to hold rates at record lows at least through mid-2013. USD/JPY also weighed by Japan exporter sales, lingering effect form S&P's downgrade of U.S. sovereign rating, worries over euro-zone debt crisis. But USD/JPY downside limited by yen-funded carry trades amid improved investor risk appetite (VIX fear gauge fell 26.96% to 35.06) as U.S. stocks closed sharply higher overnight (DJIA up 3.98%, Nasdaq up 5.29%) on Fed's ultra-loose monetary stance; Japan importer demand; expectations of Japan MOF JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Yen crosses vulnerable to \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  July trade balance data. Other data: Data focus: 2350 GMT Japan June tertiary industry index, July corporate goods price index, 1400 GMT U.S. June wholesale trade. USD/JPY daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics in bearish mode. Support at 76.70 (yesterday's low); breach would expose downside to 76.29-76.25 band (Aug. 1 low-March 17 record low), then psychological 76.00 and 75.00 levels. Resistance at 77.51 (hourly chart), then at 77.86 (yesterday's high); breach would expose upside to 78.48 (Monday's high), then 79.42 (Friday's high) and 80.25 (Thursday's high).\par \par \uc2 EUR/USD - to consolidate with bullish bias after rising strongly post-FOMC. Underpinned by weak USD sentiment, improved investor risk appetite, sovereign demand for euro; ECB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets yesterday for second straight day to buy Spanish and Italian government bonds. But EUR/USD gains tempered by worries over euro-zone sovereign debt crisis as EU leaders lacked agreement to resolve the region's fiscal woes; fears that France may be downgraded from its triple-A rating. Data focus: 0600 GMT German July CPI, 1000 GMT German 3Q Ifo economic climate for euro area. EUR/USD daily chart positive-biased as MACD & stochastics have turned bullish. Resistance at 1.4402 (hourly chart), then at 1.4432 (Monday's high) and 1.4454 (Aug. 1 high); breach would expose upside to 1.4537 (July 27 reaction high), then 1.4577 (July 4 reaction high). Support at 1.4195 (hourly chart), then at 1.4152 (yesterday's low) and 1.4129 (Monday's low); breach would expose downside to 1.4055 (Friday's low), then 1.4009 (July 18 reaction low), 1.3943 (200-day moving average) and 1.3835 (July 12 reaction low).\par \par \uc2 AUD/USD - to consolidate with risks skewed higher after strong post-FOMC rise. Underpinned by weak USD sentiment, improved investor risk appetite, AUD-USD interest rate differential, sovereign demand for Aussie. But AUD/USD gains tempered by worries over euro-zone debt crisis; concern over slower China economic growth as Beijing tightens monetary policy to combat inflation. Data focus: 0030 GMT August \uc2 Westpac\uc2 -Melbourne Institute consumer sentiment, 0130 GMT Australian June lending finance, 0400 GMT August DEEWR monthly leading indicator of employment. Daily chart mixed as MACD bearish, but stochastics have turned bullish at oversold. Resistance at 1.0445 (Monday's high); breach would expose upside to 1.0526 (Friday's high), then 1.0631 (100-day moving average) and 1.0668 (55-day moving average). Support at 1.0062 (hourly chart); breach would expose downside to 0.9924 (yesterday's low), then 0.9750 (uptrend line from March 4, 2009 low of 0.6283 on weekly chat), 0.9704 (March 17 low) and 0.9535 (Dec. 1 low).\par \par \uc2 NZD/USD - to consolidate with risks skewed higher after strong gains post-FOMC. Underpinned by weak USD sentiment, improved investor risk appetite, NZD-USD yield gap. But NZD/USD gains tempered by worries over euro-zone debt crisis, concern over slower China economic growth. Daily chart mixed as MACD bearish, but stochastics have turned bullish at oversold. Resistance at 0.8438 (Monday's high); breach would target 0.8465 (Friday's high), then 0.8678 (Aug. 3 high) and 0.8784 (Aug. 2 high). Support at 0.8066 (hourly chart); breach would expose downside to 0.7959 (yesterday's low), then 0.7854 (May 23 low) and 0.7751 (May 16 reaction low).\par \par \uc2 GBP/USD - to range-trade. Underpinned by weak USD sentiment, improved investor risk appetite. But GBP sentiment hurt by UK riots, unexpected 0.3% on-year drop in UK June industrial production (vs forecast for 0.2% rise); wider-than-expected UK June global goods trade deficit of GBP8.9 billion (vs GBP8.1 billion forecast); GBP sales on rebounding EUR/GBP cross. Data focus: 0830 GMT UK June CML regulated mortgage survey, 0930 GMT BOE inflation report. Daily chart negative-biased as stochastics falling from overbought; MACD staging bearish crossover against its exponential moving average. Support at 1.6174 (yesterday's low); breach would expose downside to 1.6120 (July 21 low), then 1.6087 (200-day moving average) and 1.6003 (July 18 reaction low, roughly matching psychological 1.6000 line). Resistance at 1.6410 (yesterday's high), then at 1.6470 (hourly chart) and 1.6510 (Monday's high); breach would target 1.6546 (May 31 reaction high), then 1.6745 (April 28 top).\par \par \uc2 USD/CHF - to consolidate with bearish bias after hitting record low of 0.7068 on EBS yesterday. Undermined by weak USD sentiment, CHF demand on soft EUR/CHF cross as worries persist over euro-zone debt crisis. But USD/CHF losses tempered by expectations of SNB's CHF-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or other measures from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap CHF strength. Daily chart negative-biased as MACD bearish, while stochastics stay suppressed at oversold; 5- & 15-day moving averages falling. Support at 0.7068 (yesterday's low); breach would expose downside to psychological round-numbered levels from 0.7000 down to 0.6400 (projected base of long-term descending channel from July 2001 high of 1.8216). Resistance at 0.7325 (hourly chart), then at 0.7447 (hourly chart); breach would expose upside to 0.7592 (yesterday's high), then 0.7653 (Monday's high), 0.7740 (Friday's high) and 0.7802 (Thursday's high).\par \par \uc2 USD/CAD - to consolidate with risks skewed lower after falling sharply from 0.9906 post-FOMC. Undermined by firmer oil prices (Nymex crude last up $2.40 at $81.70/bbl on Globex), improved investor risk appetite, weak USD sentiment. But USD/CAD losses tempered by worries over euro-zone debt crisis. USD/CAD daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics turned bearish at overbought. Support at 0.9740 (Friday's low); breach would expose downside to 0.9684 (Thursday's low), then 0.9600 (psychological level) and 0.9564 (Aug. 3 low). Resistance at 0.9956 (hourly chart); breach would expose upside to 1.0009 (yesterday's high), then 1.0057 (Jan. 31 reaction high) and 1.0110 (Dec. 27 high).\par \par \uc2 EUR/JPY - to consolidate. Underpinned by improved investor risk appetite, expectations of Japan MOF JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japan importer demand. But EUR/JPY topside limited by Japan exporter sales, worries over euro-zone sovereign debt crisis. Daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics in bearish mode. Support at 110.24 (hourly chart); breach would expose downside to 109.23 (hourly chart), then 109.10-109.06 band (yesterday's low-Aug. 3 low), 108.73 (Aug. 1 low) and 106.50 (March 17 bottom). Resistance at 112.68 (Monday's high); breach would expose upside to 113.85 (200-day moving average), then 114.16 (Thursday's high, near 55-day moving average).\par \par \uc2 EUR/GBP - to trade with bullish bias. Daily chart positive-biased as stochastics rising from oversold; MACD staging bullish crossover against its exponential moving average. Resistance at 0.8847 (July 27 high); breach would expose upside to 0.8883 (July 26 high), then 0.9000 (July 8 high). Support at 0.8755 (hourly chart); breach would expose downside to 0.8675 (yesterday's low), then 0.8660 (Monday's low), 0.8640 (Friday's low) and 0.8606 (May 26 swing low).\par \par \uc2 -By Jerry Tan, Dow Jones Newswires; (65) 6415-4046; Jerry.tan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 This is a financial news and information service. It is provided in general terms and does not take account of or address any individual user's position. To the extent that this article includes suggestions as to various possible investment strategies which users might consider, it does so in only general terms without reference to the personal factors which should determine any user's investment decisions. Nothing contained in this service constitutes personalized investment advice. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors shall not be made the basis for