\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 704 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2011\par 14:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  AIMS TO DOUBLE TRADE FINANCE REVENUE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  aims to double its revenue from trade finance to $5 billion in the coming years, as it seeks to take advantage of booming trade in fast-growing emerging markets, a senior executive at the bank says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF SHINOHARA EXPECTS GLOBAL ECONOMY TO PICK UP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The global economy has hit a "soft patch" due to unexpected weakness in the U.S. and Japan, although Germany and France are driving European growth despite the region's debt crisis, a top IMF official says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BARCLAYS TO REPAY ALL PRE-APRIL PPI CLAIMS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  will reimburse all customers who complained about mis-sold payment protection insurance before April 20, as a gesture of goodwill for those whose claims had been put on hold pending the outcome of a legal case.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES ADD TO MODEST GAINS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock futures push higher as deal news buoys sentiment, although investors remain cautious after a brutal bout of selling last week on lingering worries over global economic growth and European sovereign debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITI KEPT CLIENTS IN DARK ON HACKING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citi waited as long as three weeks to notify credit-card customers of a hacking attack because it was conducting an investigation and producing replacement cards, a person familiar with the situation tells The Wall Street Journal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLENCORE CONSIDERS GBP12B ENRC TAKEOVER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commodities trading giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Glencore\f28 \uc2 \f2  is considering a GBP12 billion takeover of London-listed miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Eurasian Natural Resources\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Sunday Times reports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NYMEX WEAKER AS SAUDI OIL PLEDGE FEEDS INTO MARKET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude prices are lower as Saudi Arabia's pledge to supply more oil to buyers in July continues to weaken prices, coupled with bearish Japanese and Chinese lending data and worries over a global economic slowdown.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ TO WEIGH FURTHER MONETARY EASING AT MEETING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan starts a two-day policy meeting and sources close to the matter say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will consider further steps to ease monetary conditions, Kyodo News reports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL SUGGESTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUND \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should set up a new fund or use fiscal receipts to conduct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , rather than printing yuan to buy up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a PBOC official and a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TWO CHINA FIRMS DELAY DOLLAR BONDS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two China-based companies have put their U.S. dollar bond issues on ice, as debt market sentiment is hit by a widening controversy over questionable accounting practices at certain Chinese firms.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Morning Briefing \par ONGOING CAUTION TO CAP STOCK GAINS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks are expected to open a few points higher as traders bet that buyers will creep back to the market on hopes that a rally is overdue, after six consecutive negative weeks, says David Morrison at spreadbettor GFT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Money Talks \par WHEN THE CAN GETS TO THE END OF THE ROAD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since the Lehman bankruptcy, policymakers on both sides of the Atlantic have gone to extremes to buy time. But with inflation picking up and government deficits hitting breaking point, the scope for endless can kicking is shrinking, writes Alen Mattich.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Analysis \par EQUITY DERIVATIVE EXPIRY TO IMPACT MARKETS, BOOST TRADE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday sees the expiration of June equity index futures contracts, index options and single-stock options in Europe, while in the U.S., single-stock futures also expire. And this could boost both volumes and intra-day volatility.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Focus \par STERLING HAS BECOME AN EVEN RISKIER BET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The stakes in sterling are rising ever higher. For the moment, the pound remains resilient against the euro and the dollar, Nicholas Hastings writes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES PUSH HIGHER ON DEAL NEWS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US stock futures add to gains as deal news boosts sentiment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US TREASURYS BARELY CHANGED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US Treasurys are stable in line with stronger bunds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWISS FRANC BENEFITS IN THIN HOLIDAY TRADING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The safe-haven Swiss franc is the standout performer in European trading hours.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE FALLS ON UNCERTAINTY OVER OIL DEMAND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. oil prices are lower as Saudi Arabia's pledge to supply more oil to buyers in July continues to weaken prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPOT GOLD SLIPS, SEEN LACKING MOMENTUM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold slips as the euro softens against the dollar. [ 13-06-11 1200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110613e76d000sf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
