\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For June 13\b0\par\par\uc2 2,047 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2011\par 09:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN CORE MACHINERY ORDERS POST SURPRISE DECLINE OF 3.3% IN APRIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese core machinery orders posted an unexpected 3.3% drop from a month earlier in April on the back of a decline in demand from manufacturers, the Cabinet Office said Monday. (published 0109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA MAY NEW YUAN LOANS DROP, MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH SLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese banks extended fewer new yuan loans in May, and money supply growth slowed, showing the impact of monetary tightening in the world's second-largest economy. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: CHINA SCHOLAR: MUST ELIMINATE ONE-WAY BET ON YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China needs to eliminate expectations of a steady appreciation of the yuan and avoid a one-way bet on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that has attracted "hot money," an influential academic said. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD GURRIA: CONCERTED POLICY DECISION BY CHINA TO EASE GROWTH PACE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese authorities are making concerted efforts to cool the country's economic growth, Angel Gurria, the Secretary General of the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development, said Monday. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL: CHINA SHOULD SET UP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUND TO CURB INFLATION \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should set up a stabilization fund to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to keep the yuan's exchange rate within a target range, a move that would curb inflation, a local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official wrote in a commentary piece on Monday. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: SHOULD USE FISCAL RECEIPTS TO MAINTAIN STABLE YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should rely more on fiscal receipts rather than printing money to maintain the stability of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Zhou Qiren, an adviser to the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said in an article on his personal website Monday. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA INTEREST RATE HIKE NEEDED AS PRICES RISE - PBOC-BACKED NEWSPAPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another interest rate hike in China is still needed as food and non-food prices continue to rise, a commentary piece in a newspaper backed by China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  argued Monday. (published 0026 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA WELL POISED TO SUSTAIN HIGH ECONOMIC GROWTH - FINANCE MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India is poised to sustain a high rate of economic expansion for some years as the country has the growth drivers in place, despite signals that the pace of factory output growth is weakening, Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee said Monday. (published 0523 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA FINANCE SECRETARY: TAX REFUND SCHEME FOR EXPORTERS EXTENDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India has extended a tax refund scheme offered to exporters until Sept. 30, Finance Secretary Sunil Mitra said Monday. (published 0444 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: TO RUN MACRO POLICIES SUCH AS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , POLICY RATE 'FLEXIBLY' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan said Monday that the authorities will continue to prioritize price stability when operating the macroeconomic policies. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA BANKS' SHORT-TERM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  BORROWING ROLLOVER RATE UP IN MAY VS APRIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The proportion of short-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  borrowings rolled over by South Korean banks rose substantially in May from the previous month but fell short of fully replacing maturing debt, the Financial Supervisory Service said Monday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE PURISIMA: PESO MARKET-DETERMINED, BUT WON'T ALLOW DISRUPTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine authorities will largely let markets determine the peso exchange rate but will act against any "disruptive" moves, especially speculative capital inflows, Finance Secretary Cesar V. Purisima said Monday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: NEW ZEALAND'S CHRISTCHURCH RATTLED BY STRONG EARTHQUAKES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's second largest city Christchurch was rocked by several strong tremors Monday, causing further damage to the already earthquake-devastated city. (published 0636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NZ MAY MEDIAN HOUSE PRICE NZ$350,000 VS NZ$360,000 IN APRIL - REINZ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand home prices fell in May from April, data from the Real Estate Institute of New Zealand showed Monday. (published 0602 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA TO RAISE UP TO $2 BLN VIA GLOBAL SUKUK ISSUE - \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia is planning to raise up to $2 billion via an issue of global sukuk, or Islamic bonds, Mukhtar Hussain, chief executive of \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Bank Malaysia Berhad\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Monday. (published 0612 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANEKA TAMBANG TO OFFER UP TO $1B BONDS IN 2H - CFO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold and nickel producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Aneka Tambang\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to offer up to $1 billion worth of bonds next month, or in the second half of the year, to finance the construction of a nickel smelter in Halmahera Island, a company executive said Monday. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TWO CHINESE FIRMS DELAY US DOLLAR BOND SALES ON MARKET WEAKNESS, ACCOUNTING WOES - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two Chinese firms have put their U.S. dollar bond sales on hold because of the market's recent weakness, driven in large part by investor concern over questionable accounting and corporate governance issues at some overseas-listed mainland companies, people familiar with the situation said Monday. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BIOSENSORS INTERNATIONAL BUYS 50% STAKE IN STENT MAKER IN S$625.4 MLN DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Biosensors International Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will acquire the remaining 50% equity stake in JW Medical Systems Ltd. from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shandong Weigao Group Medical Polymer Company Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to make the stent maker a fully-owned unit of the Singapore-listed company. (published 0016 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: MAYBANK TO MAKE OFFER TO BUY \f28 \uc2 \f2 RHB CAPITAL\f28 \uc2 \f2  BY MONTH'S END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malayan Banking Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Malaysia's largest lender by assets, Monday said it will bid for smaller rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 RHB Capital Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . by the end of this month as it seeks to expand its footprint across Southeast Asia. (published 0554 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA EVERBRIGHT BANK MAY POSTPONE HK IPO PRE-MARKETING TO TUESDAY - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Everbright Bank Co., which plans to launch an initial public offering in Hong Kong next month to raise around US$7 billion, may postpone the pre-marketing for the IPO to Tuesday from Monday due to recent market weakness, people familiar with the situation said. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: HANWHA, MERCK IN $720 MLN DEAL TO SELL BIOSIMILAR DRUGS GLOBALLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hanwha Chemical Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has signed a $720 million deal with a subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Merck & Co Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to develop and sell its biosimilar pharmaceutical products in the global market. (published 0619 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HYOSUNG CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2 : GOT $1.8 BILLION STEEL CORD SUPPLY CONTRACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyosung Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it signed a $1.8 billion contract to supply steel cord to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goodyear Tire & Rubber Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., and that it aims for a market share of more than 10% of the global steel cord market late this year through acquisitions of two steel cord plants from the U.S. tire maker. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: AIRLINES CANCEL AUSTRALASIAN FLIGHTS DUE TO ASH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volcanic ash from an eruption in Chile continues to disrupt flights in New Zealand, southern Australia and international flights out of the region as airlines cancel services on safety concerns. (published 0336 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par POSCO PLANS TO SEEK IPO FOR CHINA JV IN HONG KONG OR SHANGHAI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Posco said Monday it is planning to seek an initial public offering for Zhangjiagang Pohang Stainless Steel, a joint venture set up with a Chinese company in 1997, either in Hong Kong or Shanghai after 2013 in order to strengthen the company's value. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA HANKING STARTS HK IPO PRE-MARKETING MONDAY - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Hanking Holdings Ltd. started pre-marketing its Hong Kong initial public offering Monday ahead of a listing on the city's stock exchange in early or mid-July, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0203 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWTON RESOURCES PLANS TO RAISE UP TO US$301 MLN IN HK IPO - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese iron-ore miner Newton Resources Ltd. plans to raise up to US$301 million in an initial public offering ahead of its listing in Hong Kong on June 30, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Monday. (published 0220 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: 10 DEUTSCHE SECURITIES KOREA EMPLOYEES HAVE RESIGNED - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ten employees of Deutsche Securities Korea have resigned from the securities arm of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a person familiar with the situation said Monday, a move that comes as the unit serves a partial suspension of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after being sanctioned by local regulators earlier this year on charges of stock manipulation. (published 0348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BHP BILLITON TO BE HIT BY STRIKE AFTER OFFER TO UNIONS REJECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that rolling strikes at its coal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Australia's resource-rich Bowen Basin are set to go ahead this week after labor unions rejected an offer to hold paid meetings with members during normal working hours to discuss a pay dispute. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: MARVELL TECHNOLOGY GROUP CEO: WEAKER DOLLAR, GOLD PRICES, IMPACTING COSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The weaker U.S. dollar and high gold prices are making it more expensive to produce microchips and hurting profits, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marvell Technology Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive Sehat Sutardja. (published 0543 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MITSUBISHI MOTORS\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXPECTS 28% RISE IN NET PROFIT THIS FY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Motors Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it expects its net profit to rise 28% in the current fiscal year, as it plans to ramp up production in the second half to make up for lost output after the March 11 earthquake and expects sales in southeast Asia to help cushion the yen's strength. (published 0505 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MARUTI SUZUKI MULLS ACCEPTING NEW UNION TO END WORKERS' STRIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A workers' strike at one of the factories of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Maruti Suzuki India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . stalled production for the eighth working day Monday, even as the company's management softened its stand and said it would consider acknowledging a new employees' union. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA OFFICIAL: POSCO LAND BUYING PUT OFF TILL JUNE 17 DUE TO LOCAL FESTIVAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 13-06-11 0703GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Posco will continue to buy land for its proposed $12-billion steel plant from June 17 after a four-day break due to a local festival, an official in the eastern Indian state of Orissa said Monday. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES DOWN; WEAK TOYOTA FORECAST WEIGHS TOKYO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian shares were lower Monday, with Japan's market facing pressure from a weaker-than-expected forecast from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2 , while the New Zealand dollar tumbled on news of large aftershocks hitting Christchurch. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: DELAYED FUKUSHIMA WATER DECONTAMINATION SYSTEM TO START BY WEEKEND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it expects a newly developed system for treating highly radioactive water at its stricken Fukushima Daiichi plant to start full \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the end of this week, amid renewed concern that contaminated water may leak from the plant, causing further damage to the environment. (published 0627 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN UTILITIES' MAY OIL, LNG USE UP; NUCLEAR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese utilities consumed more fossil fuels in May than a year ago as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates fell at nuclear plants amid concerns over safety, data from the Federation of Electric Power Companies of Japan showed Monday. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA MAY CRUDE OUTPUT, REFINERY RUNS UP ON YEAR; FUEL STOCKS RISE -NDRC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's May crude-oil output and refinery runs rose modestly from a year ago, while oil product stocks continued to climb, the National Development and Reform Commission said Monday citing industry data. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA MAY NATURAL GAS IMPORTS MORE THAN DOUBLE ON YEAR -NDRC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's natural gas imports in May more than doubled from a year earlier to meet robust demand for the cleaner-burning fuel, the National Development and Reform Commission said Monday, citing industry data. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 FORTESCUE METALS\f28 \uc2 \f2  WARNS AUSTRALIA TAX WILL HIT SMALLER MINERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fortescue Metals Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Australia's third-largest iron-ore producer by output, Monday criticised the country's plans to impose a 30% tax on iron-ore and coal-mining profits, saying it is a "penalty" against smaller and emerging companies and will impact them much more than larger multinational rivals. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA IRON ORE PRICES REBOUND; STEEL OUTPUT STILL STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot iron ore prices have risen to $180 a metric ton, including the cost of freight, due to continued demand from Chinese steelmakers, Metal Bulletin data showed Monday. (published 0315 GMT) [ 13-06-11 0703GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110613e76d000ft\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
