\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 865 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2011\par 08:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN CORE MACHINERY ORDERS POST SURPRISE DECLINE OF 3.3% IN APRIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese core machinery orders posted an unexpected 3.3% drop from a month earlier in April on the back of a decline in demand from manufacturers, the Cabinet Office said Monday. (published 0109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA MAY NEW YUAN LOANS DROP, MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH SLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese banks extended fewer new yuan loans in May, and money supply growth slowed, showing the impact of monetary tightening in the world's second-largest economy. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: CHINA SCHOLAR: MUST ELIMINATE ONE-WAY BET ON YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China needs to eliminate expectations of a steady appreciation of the yuan and avoid a one-way bet on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that has attracted "hot money," an influential academic said. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD GURRIA: CONCERTED POLICY DECISION BY CHINA TO EASE GROWTH PACE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese authorities are making concerted efforts to cool the country's economic growth, Angel Gurria, the Secretary General of the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development, said Monday. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL: CHINA SHOULD SET UP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUND TO CURB INFLATION \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should set up a stabilization fund to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to keep the yuan's exchange rate within a target range, a move that would curb inflation, a local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official wrote in a commentary piece on Monday. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA OFFICIAL: ASSET BUBBLE RISKS, INFLATION PUT PRESSURE ON HK ECONOMIC HEALTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Risks of an asset bubble and rising inflation are putting pressure on the health of Hong Kong's financial system and its economy, a senior Chinese official warned Monday. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: SHOULD USE FISCAL RECEIPTS TO MAINTAIN STABLE YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should rely more on fiscal receipts rather than printing money to maintain the stability of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Zhou Qiren, an adviser to the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said in an article on his personal website Monday. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA INTEREST RATE HIKE NEEDED AS PRICES RISE - PBOC-BACKED NEWSPAPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another interest rate hike in China is still needed as food and non-food prices continue to rise, a commentary piece in a newspaper backed by China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  argued Monday. (published 0026 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA WELL POISED TO SUSTAIN HIGH ECONOMIC GROWTH - FINANCE MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India is poised to sustain a high rate of economic expansion for some years as the country has the growth drivers in place, despite signals that the pace of factory output growth is weakening, Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee said Monday. (published 0523 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA FINANCE SECRETARY: TAX REFUND SCHEME FOR EXPORTERS EXTENDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India has extended a tax refund scheme offered to exporters until Sept. 30, Finance Secretary Sunil Mitra said Monday. (published 0444 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: TO RUN MACRO POLICIES SUCH AS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , POLICY RATE 'FLEXIBLY' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan said Monday that the authorities will continue to prioritize price stability when operating the macroeconomic policies. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA BANKS' SHORT-TERM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  BORROWING ROLLOVER RATE UP IN MAY VS APRIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The proportion of short-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  borrowings rolled over by South Korean banks rose substantially in May from the previous month but fell short of fully replacing maturing debt, the Financial Supervisory Service said Monday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE PURISIMA: PESO MARKET-DETERMINED, BUT WON'T ALLOW DISRUPTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine authorities will largely let markets determine the peso exchange rate but will act against any "disruptive" moves, especially speculative capital inflows, Finance Secretary Cesar V. Purisima said Monday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NZ PRIME MINISTER: UNLIKELY TO SUPPORT COMMON PACIFIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 A common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the Pacific is unlikely to get the go ahead, with the New Zealand Prime Minister John Key Monday saying the country would probably not support such a move. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: SLUGGISH HIRING SEEN AS A THREAT TO US RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The potential for a persistent slowdown in hiring is the biggest threat to the U.S. recovery, according to economists in the latest Wall Street Journal economic forecasting survey, as they sharply cut the number of jobs they projected the economy would create in coming months. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: BOND MARKETS RATTLED BY LEHMAN AGAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nearly three years after its collapse threatened the global financial system, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . can still move markets. This time, it is the battered municipal-bond market. (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STRONG AFTERSHOCKS RATTLE NEW ZEALAND'S CHRISTCHURCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's second largest city Christchurch was hit by several strong aftershocks Monday, causing further damage to the already earthquake-devastated city. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: EUR UNDER THE COSH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: Renewed EUR bear pressure on support at 1.4285 is expected, as the powerful downtrend off the June 7 reaction high at 1.4696 looks to extend. The 1.618 Fibonacci extension target at 1.4265 will provide some support, to protect the next layer of support at 1.4135. Corrective gains are limited to the 1.4445 area, and only above there would lift the bearish EUR outlook. (published 0701 GMT) [ 13-06-11 0656GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110613e76d000f5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
