\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For May 9\b0\par\par\uc2 1,932 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2011\par 09:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ SEES POSITIVE EFFECTS FROM POST-QUAKE ASSET BUYING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Doubling the size of the Bank of Japan's asset-purchase program in the wake of the March 11 earthquake and tsunami helped to stabilize the country's financial markets and prevent corporate sentiment from worsening, members of the BOJ board said at their April 6-7 policy-setting meeting. (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC MAY RESUME 3-YEAR BOND SALE IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THIS WEEK - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may resume selling three-year bonds in its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week, in its latest effort to siphon excess liquidity out of the financial system and head off long-term inflationary pressures, traders participating in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESEARCHER: PBOC SHOULD REDUCE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should reduce its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and widen the yuan's daily trading band against the U.S. dollar to let the market have a greater say in the yuan's valuation, a researcher with Chinese Academy of Social Science, a government think tank, wrote in an article published on Caijing Magazine Monday. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PM GILLARD FACES BIG TEST IN AUSTRALIAN BUDGET BATTLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's government will likely stick with plans for a quick return to surplus in the annual budget this week largely through a mixture of higher revenues from mining exports and spending cuts, even as parts of the economy suffer under the weight of natural disasters, a soaring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and rising prices. (published 0057 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN APRIL BUSINESS CONDITIONS, CONFIDENCE DECLINE - NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian economy remained steady in April after a weak start to the year, though the rising Australian dollar and the potential for further interest-rate hikes weighed on sentiment. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANZ AUSTRALIA TOTAL JOB ADS ROSE 1.0% IN APRIL VS MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The total number of job advertisements in Australian newspapers and on the internet rose 1.0% in seasonally adjusted terms in April from March, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., which compiles the data from major newspapers, said Monday. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SINGAPORE GIC: RISK OF MAJOR ECON CRISIS IF US BONDS LOSE AAA RATING IN DISORDERLY MANNER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Government of Singapore Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Deputy Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tony Tan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that a major financial and economic crisis could erupt if the U.S. loses its AAA credit rating in a disorderly manner, while significant structural problems still plague the global economy. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOT: LIMITED IMPACT ON PROPERTY SECTOR FROM GOVERNMENT LOAN PROGRAM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai government's recently approved THB25 billion package aimed at offering cheaper housing loans is unlikely to have a significant impact on the property sector, Bank of Thailand Office of Macroeconomic Policy and Analysis Director Songtum Pinto said Monday. (published 0658 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ENN ENERGY SELLS $750M 10-YEAR GLOBAL DOLLAR BOND AT 6.098% YIELD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENN Energy Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has sold US$750 million of 10-year senior notes at 99.274 to yield 6.098%, a person familiar with the deal said Monday. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STANDARD CHARTERED PLANS BENCHMARK GLOBAL DOLLAR BOND SOON - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard Chartered Bank is planning to sell a five-year benchmark global dollar bond "as soon as possible," a person familiar with the proposed deal said Monday. (published 0056 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SHANSHUI PLANS GLOBAL DOLLAR BOND, ROADSHOW THROUGH MAY 17 - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Shanshui Cement Group Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to sell a global dollar bond after holding a roadshow through May 17, a person familiar with the proposed deal said Monday. (published 0451 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA LIANSU GROUP SELLS $300 MLN 5-YEAR GLOBAL DOLLAR BOND AT 99.493 TO YIELD 8.0% - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Liansu Group has sold a $300 million five-year global dollar bond at 99.493 to yield 8.0%, a person familiar with the deal said Monday. (published 0131 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: HONG KONG 1Q ECONOMIC GROWTH LIKELY EASED TO 5.3% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's economy likely continued to expand in the first quarter, supported by solid domestic and external demand, though at a slower pace than the previous quarter due to a higher base of comparison. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CARLYLE, MACQUARIE NOT CONSIDERING HIGHER BID FOR REDFLEX -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Carlyle Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Macquarie Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . aren't considering raising their offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Redflex Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . after the red-light and speed infringement camera group's shareholders voted against the pair's A$303.5 million takeover bid, a person familiar with the matter said Monday. (published 0314 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPOTLESS GETS A$656.9M TAKEOVER APPROACH FROM PRIVATE EQUITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian cleaning company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Spotless Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has rejected a A$656.9 million takeover offer from a private equity firm. (published 2249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MGM CHINA STARTS PRE-MARKETING MONDAY FOR UP TO US$1.5 BLN HK IPO - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MGM China Holdings Ltd., a gambling joint venture between \f28 \uc2 \f2 MGM Resorts International\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the daughter of gambling tycoon Stanley Ho, has started pre-marketing for a Hong Kong initial public offering that will raise US$1 billion-US$1.5 billion, a person familiar with the situation said Monday. (published 0222 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SANDS CHINA IFRS 1ST-QUARTER NET PROFIT MORE THAN DOUBLES TO US$262.4 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sands China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its first-quarter net profit more than doubled from a year earlier, boosted by soaring gambling revenue growth in Macau. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHENZHEN INTERNATIONAL RAISES STAKE IN SHENZHEN AIRLINES FOR CNY788.6M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shenzhen International Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Sunday it has agreed to raise its stake in Shenzhen Airlines Ltd. to 49% for CNY788.6 million . (published 0010 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TULLY SUGAR TAKEOVER TUSSLE HOTS UP; CHINA'S COFCO TO BID - TULLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A takeover tussle for unlisted Australian miller \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tully Sugar Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is hotting up with the company reporting Friday that state-owned trading concern Cofco Corp. will bid A$41 a share, valuing Tully at A$126.7 million. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOSHIBA JAN-MAR NET PFT DOUBLES, FY PFT BACK TO PRE-GLOBAL FINANCIAL CRISIS LEVEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toshiba Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that its net profit for the three months through March doubled from a year earlier, bringing its full year net profit back to its level before the global financial crisis. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOFTBANK PROFIT SURGES IN JANUARY-MARCH AS IPHONE DEMAND STILL STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Softbank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its net profit for the three months through March surged from the previous year as strong demand for the iPhone continued to boost the Japanese mobile phone carrier's revenue. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SUMITOMO CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  JANUARY-MARCH GROUP NET PROFIT Y34.2 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that its net profit for the three months ended March 31 dropped about 8%, but its outlook for the current fiscal year is for a pickup in net profit boosted by resource-related business. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: THAI UNION FROZEN 1ST-QUARTER NET FALLS 9.4%; OUTLOOK ROSY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai Union Frozen Products PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday its first-quarter net profit fell 9.4% from a year earlier even as sales rose significantly, as higher expenses and a rise in its debt-to-equity ratio weighed on profitability. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INCITEC PIVOT 1H PROFIT JUMPS 25%; LINKED TO ASIAN GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fertilizer and explosives maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Incitec Pivot Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday reported a 25% surge in first half profit to A$165.6 million from A$132.4 million, a result that Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 James Fazzino\f28 \uc2 \f2  said confirmed the value of the company's strategic alignment to the industrialization and urbanization of Asia. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OM HOLDINGS SAYS LEGAL ADVICE SUGGESTS IT CAN DUAL LIST IN HONG KONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A rejected resolution in \f28 \uc2 \f2 OM Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s annual general meeting last month is unlikely to stop the manganese miner's plan to dual-list in Hong Kong and Australia, the company said Monday. (published 0154 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGTEL NAMES TEMASEK'S SIMON ISRAEL AS CHAIRMAN TO SUCCEED CHUMPOL NALAMLIENG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Telecommunications Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that Simon Israel, currently the executive director and president of state investment firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Temasek Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2 , will succeed Chumpol NaLamlieng as chairman and director of the telecommunications company. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHANDRA ASRI PLANS TO RAISE $200 MLN VIA 20% RIGHTS ISSUE - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Chandra Asri Petrochemical\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to sell a 20% stake in itself via a rights issue to raise $200 million to finance its expansion, a company official said Monday. (published 0634 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: METRO PACIFIC INVESTMENTS 1Q NET PHP820 MLN, UP 26% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Metro Pacific Investments Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday reported first-quarter net profit growth of 26% versus a year earlier, bolstered by strong revenue contribution from its water and power distribution utilities. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANGCHAK PLANS TO BUY 40% OF THAI AGRO ENERGY FOR UP TO THB438 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bangchak Petroleum PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it plans to acquire 320 million shares, or a 40% stake, in Thai Agro Energy PCL from Lanna Resources PCL and other minority shareholders for up to THB438.4 million . (published 0648 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RELIANCE INDUSTRIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  LOOKS TO PETROCHEMICALS, RETAIL, TELECOM TO DRIVE GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reliance Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will look to its petrochemicals, consumer retail and telecommunications businesses to drive growth in the next few years, Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mukesh Ambani\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a letter to shareholders. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; TOKYO DOWN ON POWER SHORTAGE WORRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly higher Monday, but euro zone debt woes continued to temper demand, while shares in Tokyo were undermined by concerns about potential power shortages. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WORKERS SURVEY FUKUSHIMA DAIICHI REACTOR BUILDING TO PREPARE FOR REPAIR WORK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-05-11 0710GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eight workers and a government inspector entered the reactor building of the quake-hit Fukushima Daiichi nuclear complex's No. 1 unit early Monday to survey conditions inside, another step toward bringing the complex's three damaged reactors under control since they began leaking radiation after the devastating March 11 earthquake and tsunami. (published 0608 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MINERS ON ALERT FOR NEGATIVE SURPRISES IN AUSTRALIA'S BUDGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mining companies operating in Australia will be keeping a watchful eye on this week's federal budget, staying alert to further attempts by the government to leverage the commodities boom to help it return to a budget surplus. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN AGRIBUSINESS CONDITIONS DETERIORATE IN 1Q -NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian agribusiness conditions deteriorated further in the first quarter of 2011, but a quarterly survey issued Monday by \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Australia Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., showed expectations for the year are fairly optimistic based on a solid production outlook and strong demand, despite a strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDIA UNLIKELY TO ALLOW MORE SUGAR EXPORTS IN 2010-11 AS OUTPUT SLIPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India is unlikely to allow more sugar exports under the Open General Licence beyond the 500,000 metric tons permitted this marketing year as the country's output is likely to fall short of the previous estimate, industry and government officials said Monday. (published 0652 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAUDI TO SUPPLY FULL TERM VOLUMES TO ASIA FOR JUNE AS EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi Arabian Oil Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will maintain full contracted crude-oil volumes to Asian refiners in June, with some refiners continuing to get higher-than-contracted supplies of lighter grades offset by fewer heavy barrels, executives with the refiners said Monday. (published 0434 GMT) [ 09-05-11 0710GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110509e759000m3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
