\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 837 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2011\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ SEES POSITIVE EFFECTS FROM POST-QUAKE ASSET BUYING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Doubling the size of the Bank of Japan's asset-purchase program in the wake of the March 11 earthquake and tsunami helped to stabilize the country's financial markets and prevent corporate sentiment from worsening, members of the BOJ board said at their April 6-7 policy-setting meeting. (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US WILL PRESS CHINA TO HASTEN YUAN'S RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. officials will press China to allow the value of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yuan, rise more quickly, amid signs that Beijing may be deciding to move at a faster clip in part to fight inflation. (published 1852 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: US HOME VALUES TAKES A TUMBLE - ZILLOW.COM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Home values posted the largest decline in the first quarter since late 2008, prompting many economists to push back their estimates of when the housing market will hit a bottom. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESEARCHER: PBOC SHOULD REDUCE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should reduce its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and widen the yuan's daily trading band against the U.S. dollar to let the market have a greater say in the yuan's valuation, a researcher with Chinese Academy of Social Science, a government think tank, wrote in an article published on Caijing Magazine Monday. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: SINGAPORE GIC: RISK OF MAJOR ECON CRISIS IF US BONDS LOSE AAA RATING IN DISORDERLY MANNER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Government of Singapore Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Deputy Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tony Tan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that a major financial and economic crisis could erupt if the U.S. loses its AAA credit rating in a disorderly manner, while significant structural problems still plague the global economy. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PM GILLARD FACES BIG TEST IN AUSTRALIAN BUDGET BATTLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's government will likely stick with plans for a quick return to surplus in the annual budget this week largely through a mixture of higher revenues from mining exports and spending cuts, even as parts of the economy suffer under the weight of natural disasters, a soaring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and rising prices. (published 0057 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN APRIL BUSINESS CONDITIONS, CONFIDENCE DECLINE - NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian economy remained steady in April after a weak start to the year, though the rising Australian dollar and the potential for further interest-rate hikes weighed on sentiment. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ANZ AUSTRALIA TOTAL JOB ADS ROSE 1.0% IN APRIL VS MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The total number of job advertisements in Australian newspapers and on the internet rose 1.0% in seasonally adjusted terms in April from March, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., which compiles the data from major newspapers, said Monday. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC MAY RESUME 3-YEAR BOND SALE IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THIS WEEK - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may resume selling three-year bonds in its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week, in its latest effort to siphon excess liquidity out of the financial system and head off long-term inflationary pressures, traders participating in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SPAIN TO CUT EUR2B MORE IN SPENDING IF GDP GROWTH ESTIMATE MISSED-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spain will have to cut public spending by an additional EUR2 billion if it misses its 2011 gross domestic product growth estimate of 1.3%, reports El Pais in its Monday Internet edition, citing the Economy Ministry. (published 0104 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: ENN ENERGY SELLS $750M 10-YEAR GLOBAL DOLLAR BOND AT 6.098% YIELD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENN Energy Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has sold US$750 million of 10-year senior notes at 99.274 to yield 6.098%, a person familiar with the deal said Monday. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par STANDARD CHARTERED PLANS BENCHMARK GLOBAL DOLLAR BOND SOON - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard Chartered Bank is planning to sell a five-year benchmark global dollar bond "as soon as possible," a person familiar with the proposed deal said Monday. (published 0056 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SHANSHUI PLANS GLOBAL DOLLAR BOND, ROADSHOW THROUGH MAY 17 - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Shanshui Cement Group Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to sell a global dollar bond after holding a roadshow through May 17, a person familiar with the proposed deal said Monday. (published 0451 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA LIANSU GROUP SELLS $300 MLN 5-YEAR GLOBAL DOLLAR BOND AT 99.493 TO YIELD 8.0% - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Liansu Group has sold a $300 million five-year global dollar bond at 99.493 to yield 8.0%, a person familiar with the deal said Monday. (published 0131 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par PREVIEW: HONG KONG 1Q ECONOMIC GROWTH LIKELY EASED TO 5.3% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's economy likely continued to expand in the first quarter, supported by solid domestic and external demand, though at a slower pace than the previous quarter due to a higher base of comparison. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: CHANCES SINK FOR YUAN FLOAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another meeting of the U.S.-China Strategic & Economic Dialogue, another brief surge for the yuan. (published 1554 GMT) [ 09-05-11 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110509e7590008i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
