\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Researcher: PBOC Should Reduce  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market\b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2011\par 04:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should reduce its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and widen the yuan's daily trading band against the U.S. dollar to let the market have a greater say in the yuan's valuation, a researcher with Chinese Academy of Social Science, a government think tank, wrote in an article published on Caijing Magazine Monday.\par \par \uc2 Zhang Ming, deputy director of the research section for international finance, said China is facing a tough challenge of restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  accumulation, which has become major source of the excess liquidity in China.\par \par \uc2 Zhang said China should also strictly supervise capital inflows, reduce the preferential policies for foreign direct investment and encourage Chinese companies to expand overseas investment.\par \par \uc2 In another article also published on Caijing Magazine Monday, Chen Daofu, policy research chief at the Financial Research Institute of the State Council's Development Research Center, wrote that China should consider establishing several different organizations to manage the large amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 The State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently oversees the country's reserves.\par \par \uc2 "It's inadequate to let only one organization to decide how to use the $3 trillion worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, and to ensure its liquidity and security," Chen wrote in the article.\par \par \uc2 China should set up a national committee in charge of overseas resources investment as soon as possible and intensify the effort to import strategically important resources like oil and coal.\par \par \uc2 -Yajun Zhang contributed to this article, Dow Jones Newswires; (86 10) 8400-7712; yajun.zhang@dowjones.com [ 09-05-11 0217GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110509e7590003u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
