\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/CNY Down After Record Low Parity;6.5320 Support\b0\par\par\uc2 1,755 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2011\par 04:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0228 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/CNY is lower, following the fifth consecutive record low central parity set by the PBOC. The pair is at 6.5388 from 6.5420 late Thursday, and is tipped to find support at 6.5320, says a Shanghai-based trader at a local bank. "The pace of the yuan's appreciation has picked up recently, and it could be due to expectations for higher CPI in March. The PBOC is also known to allow the yuan to rise more ahead of important international meetings, and there are G20, and IMF meetings in Washington D.C. next week," the trader says. The central parity is set at 6.5420 from 6.5456 Thursday. (esther.fung@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0227 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PHP is sliding lower, quickly reversing gears, as EUR continued to advance in early Asian trade following the ECB's rate hike. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair is at 43.04 after settling at 43.10 late Thursday--a four-month low--and rising early to 43.13. Trading volume is moderate. "We don't think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow dollar to slip below PHP43, at least not before a weekend when (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) inflows are expected to build up," says a local bank trader. Traders expect subsequent support for the USD/PHP at 42.80, and immediate resistance at 43.30. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0227 GMT [Dow Jones] Australia's S&P/ASX 200 index is up 0.5% at 4929.5 after hitting a 7-week high of 4934.8, surprising traders who expected a flat-to-weaker performance after strong gains in recent weeks. Banks are accounting for much of the strength, with \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2  (NAB.AU) up 1.0% after \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  added NAB to its "Conviction Buy" list. Newcrest (NCM.AU) is up 1.0% as spot gold has risen 0.3% to US$1,462.09 in Asian trading. Energy stocks are also firm, with Woodside (WPL.AU) up 0.7% as Nymex May crude oil futures is up 41 cents at US$110.71 after hitting a 30-month high of US$110.83. But the buying is also fairly widespread, with Orica (ORI.AU) up 2.4%, Alumina (AWC.AU) up 2.7%, CSL (CSL.AU) up 1.3%, \uc2 Wesfarmers\uc2  (WES.AU) up 0.9%, \uc2 QR National\uc2  (QRN.AU) up 3.8% and Lynas (LYC.AU) up 6.3%. BHP (BHP.AU) is down 0.4%, with traders waiting to see whether its planned A$5 billion off-market buyback is upscaled on Monday. Telstra (TLS.AU) is another drag, down 0.9%. (david.rogers1@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0221 GMT [Dow Jones] The KLCI is off 0.1% at 1560.62, with select blue chips leading declines, says a local brokerage. "I think people are just cautious and are unlikely to want to take positions ahead of the weekend," says the dealer; he adds, the index will probably stay within a tight 1555-1565 band the rest of the day. Market breadth is mixed with 268 gainers, 204 losers and 257 counters traded unchanged on a lower volume of 350 million vs around 500 million in the first hour of trade. Among losers, \uc2 Nestle\uc2  (4707.KU) is down 1.2% at MYR47.90 IOI Corp (1961.KU) is down 0.7% at MYR5.68, Maxis (6012.KU) is down 0.6% at MYR5.37 and Tenaga (5347.KU) is down 0.5% at MYR6.16. On the upside, KPJ (5878.KU) rises 2.4% to MYR4.30, \uc2 IJM Corp\uc2  (3336.KU) is up 1.2% at MYR6.50 and Dayang (5141.KU) rises 2.4% to MYR2.16. (elffie.chew@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0215 GMT [Dow Jones] Philippine shares are a tad lower with investors starting to take profit on recent gainers as they await first quarter results, say traders. The benchmark PSEi is off 0.1% at 4217.01 after closing up 0.2% at 4219.43 Thursday, a fresh four-month high. Traders tip immediate support at 4200 and resistance at 4250. Volume is thin, with gainers still edging out decliners, albeit narrowly, 35 to 34. Jose Vistan, research head at AB Capital Securities, says the market may continue to consolidate in a narrow range until investors see first quarter results, which are expected to start trickling in the coming weeks. Investors are taking profit on utilities that recently helped the market advance such as Energy Development (EDC.PH), down 0.7% at PHP6.64, and First Gen (FGEN.PH), down 0.2% at PHP13.50. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0213 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is lower at 8,660 from 8,672 late Thursday as risk appetite improves. But dealers expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in again to buy the greenback around IDR8,650-IDR8,655, levels at which it has been suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last two days to temper volatility. "The market is testing whether Bank Indonesia will defend those levels as a support level for the dollar," a dealer says. The pair is tipped in the 8,650-8,680 range for the day. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0212 GMT [Dow Jones] LME 3-month copper is at $9,720/ton, up $50 with 1,385 lots done so far; technical momentum is intact but not everyone is convinced about this move, with fundamentals remaining impaired in the short term. "While not wishing to bang on day after day about this, the physical market remains soft. The driver is very much institutional in nature," says Sucden Financial. The stronger EUR/USD, helped by Thursday's ECB rate hike, has been a key driver of this week's gains with Shanghai copper still trading at a significant discount to LME, as it has done since August. Copper is up 3.7% for the week so far. (james.campbell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0209 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian shares are likely to rise, helped by the stronger rupiah and gains in most Asian markets, traders say. They expect the main index to test resistance at 3750 after it ends up 0.1% Thursday at 3730.583. "Any failures to break above the resistance level of 3750, however, may inspire profit-taking," says a trader with a local securities firm. Commodity-related stocks such as coal producer Bumi (BUMI.JK), CPO producer Sampoerna Agro (SGRO.JK) may lead gains on higher commodity prices, while car maker Astra (ASII.JK) may fall on further profit-taking after gaining more than 5% since the start of April. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0208 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan shares are down 0.2% at 8883.95, as investors take profit after the Taiex gained 4.1% over the past six sessions; the Taiex will likely remain rangebound in 8850-8900 for the rest of session. Grand Cathay Securities analyst Mars Hsu says "investors are taking a breather ahead of a slew of first-quarter earnings announcements starting next week, when they will seek fresh comment on the outlook for the second quarter." Among leading losers, HTC (2498.TW) is down 2.9% at NT$1,165.00, Hon Hai (2317.TW) is down 0.9% at NT$108.50 and TSMC (2330.TW) is down 0.3% at NT$72.60. Among gainers, Compal (2325.TW) is up 3.3% at NT$29.45 on its share buyback while \uc2 AU Optronics\uc2  (2409.TW) is up 1.0% at NT$25.85 on improved ASP in March. Meanwhile, Ambassador Hotel (2704.TW) rises 4.4% to NT$44.90 and Grand Formosa (2707.TW) is up 2.6% at NT$513.00, on news Taiwan will allow Chinese individual tourists to visit by end June. (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0206 GMT [Dow Jones] China government bonds are higher amid strong demand from cash-rich banks and insurers, says a Shanghai-based trader with a local broker. "Some investors expect the country's inflationary growth to peak in the first six months this year due to the impact of the latest tightening measures, and (expectations) growth is likely to slow down in the second half of the year. So they think the current bond yields are acceptable," he adds. The Shanghai Stock Exchange government bond index is at 127.71, up from Thursday's close of 127.69, and is tipped to in a 127.70-127.80 range. (ming.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0203 GMT [Dow Jones] The HSI is up 0.2% at 24,322.42, with further upside likely to be modest after it rose five out of the past six sessions, say dealers. Core Pacific-Yamaichi tips the index to remain rangebound in a 24,100-24,500 band. On individual sectors, the house expects China cement stocks to continue their outperformance on expectations of strong earnings for 1Q11 after Anhui Conch's (0914.HK) recent positive earnings guidance. Anhui is up 2.2% at HK$52.95. Henderson Land (0012.HK) is up 0.8% at HK$56.45 after chairman Lee Shau-kee further raised his stake in the company. \uc2 Cathay Pacific\uc2  (0293.HK) is down 0.3% at HK$19.26, after it raised its stake in \uc2 Air China\uc2 's (0753.HK) H-shares to 53.04% from 52.92% for around HK$39.6 million; \uc2 Air China\uc2  is up 0.3% at HK$7.31. Volume is modest at HK$11.18 billion. (susanna.tai@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0202 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/TWD falls for a fifth straight day, to 28.954 from 29.050 late Thursday, due to steady foreign inflows, says a local trader. He tips the pair is likely to trade in the 28.940-29.060 band. "Foreign investors feel Asia is a good place to park their money right now because of the overall economic growth mainly led by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." He adds unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last few minutes of the session as it's suspected to have done in the last two days, the pair could test support at 28.500 before the end of the session; the pair came off an intraday low of 28.940 Thursday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to two other traders. (jenny.hsu@dowjones.com) [ 04-07-11 2228ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110408e7480001q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
