\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 13:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 : Further Rating Cuts Can't Be Ruled Out After EU Pact \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further downgrades of European sovereigns can't be ruled out after the 27 European Union countries agreed the Euro Plus Pact on March 25, Moody's Investors Service said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF STRAUSS-KAHN: CAPITAL CONTROLS MAY BE APPROPRIATE IN SOME CIRCUMSTANCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world needs globally-agreed rules for monitoring capital flows, and the use of capital controls may be appropriate in some circumstances, International Monetary Fund Managing Director Dominique Strauss-Kahn said Thursday. (published 1152 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB WEBER: MARKETS HAVE OVERREACTED TO DEBT CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial markets have overreacted to Europe's debt crisis and are likely to continue that trend in the near term, German Bundesbank President Axel Weber said Thursday. (published 1152 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB TRICHET: ANY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WOULD NEED TO BE FULLY CONVERTIBLE, FREE FLOATING TO ENTER SDR BASKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said Thursday that the Chinese yuan, like any other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , would need to conform to several conditions to be added to the Special Drawing Rights basket. (published 1006 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU PROPOSES NEW COMMON RULES FOR MORTGAGE LENDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The European Commission proposed a new set of common rules for mortgage lending in the 27-country bloc aimed at creating a true single market for property lending and enhancing consumer protection by ensuring borrowers can pay, it said Thursday. (published 1129 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC TO CUT HK OFFSHORE YUAN INTEREST RATE TO 0.72% VS 0.99% EFFECTIVE FRIDAY - BOC HK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  will cut the offshore yuan interest rate in Hong Kong to 0.72% from 0.99% effective April 1, the city's sole clearing bank, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOC Hong Kong Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday. (published 1119 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA YUAN UP LATE ON RECORD LOW PARITY AS G-20 MEETING BEGINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's yuan rose to a record high against the U.S. dollar late Thursday after the People's Bank of China set a record-low central parity as an international financial summit began in the eastern Chinese city of Nanjing. (published 1034 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK HOUSE PRICES RISE UNEXPECTEDLY IN MARCH - NATIONWIDE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. house prices rose unexpectedly for a second consecutive month in March, but the fragile economic outlook suggests this isn't the beginning of a strong rally in prices, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nationwide Building Society\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 1009 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH 2010 DEFICIT DATA SUGGEST EU PLEDGES CAN BE KEPT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 France's 2010 budget deficit undershot initial government forecasts, suggesting the country will stick to pledges of taking its public finances shortfall below 3% within two years. (published 1005 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH FEB PPI +0.8% ON MONTH; +6.3% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French producer prices rose substantially in February, as refining and coking prices rose by a third from last year, according to data released Thursday by the French national statistics office Insee. (published 0747 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK INFLATION EXPECTATIONS EBB IN MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. public's expectations for inflation fell back slightly in March, a reassuring piece of news for policy makers at the Bank of England. (published 1039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PORTUGAL DEBT INSURANCE COSTS HIT RECORD HIGH; CDS AT 580 BPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Debt insurance costs for the weaker economies in Europe were higher Thursday, with the level for Portugal climbing to a new record high. (published 0953 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US GEITHNER ARGUES FOR FLEXIBLE EXCHANGE RATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Flexible exchange rates can help countries better absorb shocks and better tailor monetary policies to their individual circumstances, Geithner said in prepared remarks that he is to deliver at the Nanjing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seminar. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: EURO-ZONE INFLATION HITS 29-MONTH HIGH IN MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's inflation rate jumped unexpectedly to its highest level for 29 months in March, strengthening the case for the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to raise interest rates for the first time in almost three years next week, official data showed Thursday. (published 1009 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK MORTGAGE DEFAULTS UNEXPECTEDLY RISE - BOE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mortgage defaults in the U.K. increased unexpectedly in the first three months of 2011 and lenders are worried that higher interest rates will force more homeowners to default, the Bank of England said Thursday. (published 0953 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU APPROVES AUSTRIA'S PLANS TO SUPPORT KOMMUNALKREDIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European Commission approved Thursday Austrian plans to support and restructure \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kommunalkredit Austria AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , it said in a statement. (published 1050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN FINANCE MINISTER: MULTILATERAL SOLUTION NEEDED FOR DAMAGING CAPITAL FLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German Finance Minister Wolfgang Schaeuble Thursday called for a "multilateral solution" to limit the damaging consequences of volatile capital flows--a hint that Germany may accept capital controls under some circumstances, but only if they respect a strict set of rules and after a global consensus about them has been reached. (published 0930 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWEDEN TO WRITE OFF LIBERIA'S $10.6M DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swedish government Thursday decided to write off west African country Liberia's entire debt of around $10.6 million, it said in a statement. (published 1031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SARKOZY URGES GLOBAL RETHINK OF LIQUIDITY PROVISION RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French president Nicolas Sarkozy Thursday urged the group of 20 industrialized and emerging nations to seek ways to better manage global liquidity especially in times of crisis, including possibly allowing the International Monetary Fund to tap financial markets to increase its lending capacity. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: GERMANY'S MARCH ADJ JOBLESS RATE AT RECORD LOW 7.1% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany's labor market improved sharply in March and unemployment declined by more than expected, propelled by the country's economic upswing. (published 0910 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ZHOU: GLOBAL ECONOMIC ADJUSTMENT SHOULD FOCUS ON LONG TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The international community should focus on long-term reform of the international monetary system and not quick fixes, said People's Bank of China Gov. Zhou Xiaochuan Thursday in comments suggesting U.S. insistence that China allow the yuan to appreciate more quickly is misguided. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TURKISH LIRA FIRMS AFTER STRONG 4Q GDP DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkish lira firms against the dollar after data showed 4Q GDP rose 9.2% on the year. (published 0837 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RUSSIA MAY CUT 2011 FOREIGN BORROWING TO $2B-$3B FROM $7B - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will suggest halving the maximum volume of the country's foreign borrowing in 2011, Interfax quoted Deputy Finance Minister Dmitry Pankin as saying Thursday. (published 0916 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER LI: INTERNATIONAL MONETARY SYSTEM REFORM NEEDS TO BE GRADUAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A prominent Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser said Thursday reform of the international monetary system should be carried out gradually so as to minimize the negative impact on China's massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN DOESN'T PLAN TO WIDEN NUCLEAR EVACUATION ZONE DESPITE IAEA FINDINGS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan has no immediate plan to expand the evacuation zone around the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant despite a finding showing higher-than-permitted levels of radiation outside the current zone and a continued rise in radiation levels in nearby ocean water, the government said Thursday. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK CONSUMER CONFIDENCE REMAINS STEADY IN MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. consumer confidence remained steady in March as Britons became more upbeat about the outlook for the economy, but more worried about their personal finances. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN FINANCE MINISTER: PORTUGAL HAS LIMITED IMPACT ON SPAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trust by financial markets globally in the euro zone has increased in recent months as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area has moved to find solutions for its problems, German Finance Minister Wolfgang Schaeuble said Wednesday. (published 0022 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASIA CENTRAL BANKS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS US, FRANCE PRESS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ON YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea and Malaysia were seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday to slow the rise of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the yuan at a record high and the U.S. and France called for more flexibility in exchange rates--the latest sign they want Beijing to let its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise faster. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par POST-JAPAN QUAKE SURVEY SHOWS SHARP DROP IN BUSINESS CONDITIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Following the devastating earthquake that struck Japan earlier this month, manufacturing activity deteriorated at its fastest pace on record, a survey by a private research firm showed Thursday. (published 2332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  ====== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: EUR/USD SET FOR PUSH HIGHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: The euro is poised to win this intriguing two-day standoff, and a push above 1.4149 is expected to open projected resistance at 1.4188. A push through 1.4188 is required to keep the uptrend intact, opening 1.4220 and the Mar. 22 reaction high at 1.4249. The 1.4095 area will look to contain weakness, but only a break below Wednesday's 1.4052 low would concern bulls. (published 0712 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN EQUITY INDEX TECHNICALS: BULLS STILL IN CHARGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday FTSE 100: Bulls retain control of the short-term, and resistance at 5940.0 is likely to be broken. The wave equality target at 5994.0 is within reach, which lies just beneath the Mar. 4 lower high at 5996.0, and together with the psychological importance of the 6000.0 level, this area will look to protect the Feb. 21 contract high at 6042.0. Solid support at 5875.0 will look to cushion corrective weakness, but only below 5832.0 would concern bulls. (published 0713 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: CORRECTING HIGHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 31-03-11 1100GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: The recovery off 121.16 is likely to struggle, and has scope to the 121.80 area before bears look to re-emerge. The sharpness of the setback off the 122.74 high highlights the dominant bear tone, and the main threat is for a downtrend extension below 121.16 towards the Feb. 9 contract low at 120.92. A downwave equality target lies at 120.61. A break above 121.80 would provide respite, but projected resistance at 122.11 is not expected to yield. (published 0752 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN COMMODITY TECHNICALS: CRUDE/METALS TO PUSH HIGHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday Brent : Bulls are expected to force a break through $116.13, as the recovery off Tuesday's $113.52 low looks to extend. A push through $116.13 would also break a three-week bear trendline, opening $116.68 and the Mar. 18 high at $117.29. Only a break below $114.50 would suggest a return to $113.52 is on the cards. (published 0823 GMT) [ 31-03-11 1100GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110331e73v00112\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
