\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-China Money: IRS, stocks, yuan seen rising after RRR hike\b0\par\par\uc2 866 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 00:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story filed late on Friday, with no changes to text)\par \par \uc2 * Many market players had expected pause on tightening\par \par \uc2 * Chinese interest rate swaps could correct upwards\par \par \uc2 * Impact on stocks could be offset if nuclear fears subside\par \par \uc2 * Yuan could rise further as another inflation-fighting tool\par \par \uc2 By Lu Jianxin and Jason Subler\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, March 18 (Reuters) - Chinese interest rate swaps, share prices and the yuan are all expected to rise on Monday, though for different reasons, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly raised banks' reserve requirement ratios (RRR) after markets had closed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The 50 basis point increase in the proportion of deposits that banks must hold on reserve with the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC)\uc2 , the third such rise this year and the sixth since November, will catch many investors off guard. [ID:nTOE722076]\par \par \uc2 IRS and money market rates have dropped excessively over the past few weeks on the prospect the PBOC's monetary tightening might not be as harsh as the market had previously expected, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Several prominent economists had also predicted this week that the PBOC would take some time to gauge the impact of Japan's devastating earthquake and tsunami, contributing to expectations further tightening was off the cards for now.\par \par \uc2 "Few expected a RRR hike to come at this time," said Liu Junyu, senior debt market analyst at \uc2 China Merchants Bank\uc2  in Shenzhen.\par \par \uc2 "It means the government has by no means relaxed its efforts to curb inflation, no matter what has happened in Japan or whatever the market has guessed."\par \par \uc2 The benchmark five-year IRS <CNYQB7R5Y=>, which plunged 76 basis points over the past month to close at 3.7 percent on Friday, is likely to rebound to a level around 4 percent, where it may build up a floor, traders said. [CN/]\par \par \uc2 LIQUIDITY VS. NUCLEAR CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 Many had taken the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions in its open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  as another sign it might not raise required reserves or interest rates soon.\par \par \uc2 The PBOC has drained funds through bill sales and bond repurchase agreements in each of the last two weeks, raising the hope it might be able to manage liquidity without turning to the harsher tool of raising required reserves. [CN/MMT]\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be moving pre-emptively to fend off a large amount of cash that will re-enter the financial system in the next several weeks, or even through inflows of foreign capital that have not yet been reported, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Close to 750 billion yuan in PBOC bills are set to mature by the end of April, putting extra pressure on the PBOC to find ways to drain liquidity.\par \par \uc2 "It appears to be an indication that foreign capital inflows into China remain high, and there are too many maturing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills, which are pumping money into the system," said Qian Qimin, deputy head of research at Shenyin & Wanguo Securities in Shanghai.\par \par \uc2 "But the market has gotten used to such RRR hikes, and there should be no big impact on share price movements," he said.\par \par \uc2 Any negative impact on the stock market from the increase in required reserves could be offset by the fact mainland shares may have overreacted over the past week to concerns about the nuclear crisis in Japan following last week's earthquake, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Shanghai Composite Index <.SSEC> fell 0.9 percent this week, despite a flurry of record-high quarterly profits reported by many top companies over the last week. [.SS]\par \par \uc2 Should worries over the nuclear situation subside somewhat, the Chinese market could continue to edge up after rising 0.3 percent on Friday to close at 2,906.9 points, but it will likely face resistance at 3,000 points, traders said.\par \par \uc2 ROOM TO RUN FOR THE YUAN?\par \par \uc2 The signal from the PBOC that it is ready to do whatever it takes to fight inflation could also give a boost to the yuan <CNY=CFXS>, should the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wish to use it too to signal its intent to keep prices from getting out of control.\par \par \uc2 The PBOC has already allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to creep upwards this year to around 6.57 to the dollar, up nearly 4 percent since it was de-pegged last summer, in what some analysts say is a sign it is ready to use the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its anti-inflationary campaign.\par \par \uc2 More and more Chinese analysts have begun to argue that higher commodity prices warrant a further increase in the yuan's value, as it would lower the cost of imported raw materials.\par \par \uc2 Yu Yongding, a former academic adviser to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said on Friday that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  should stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the yuan steady because the cost of doing so is ballooning as rising commodity prices erode the value of the dollar and of China's vast \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. [ID:nLDE72H17O]\par \par \uc2 Several dealers said they expect the yuan to hit another few record highs next week, with one possibly on Monday, after it closed near a record high on Friday. [CNY/]\par \par \uc2 CHINA-ECONOMY/RRR-MARKETS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110323e73k001c5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
