\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Move Largely Unnoticed As Focus Is On G7 Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 12:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised the amount banks must set aside as reserves by 50 basis points Friday but the significance of the move has been lost in a market held in thrall by \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks of the Group of Seven leading industrial nations in a bid to stem the yen's sharp recent gains.\par \par \uc2 China had been expected to continue lifting this rate as it attempts to curb accelerating inflation. Friday's decision is due to take effect March 25. The last rate increase took place Feb. 24.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , raised the reserve requirement ratio six times last year, and benchmark lending and deposit rates three times since October.\par \par \uc2 "We have seen so many of these [increases] for them to have a real effect," said Elsa Lignos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Even the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which tends to be more sensitive to developments in China, namely the Australian dollar, has barely changed after the news. The Aussie eased a touch against the greenback to $0.99.\par \par \uc2 -By Siva Sithraputhran, Dow Jones Newswires, +44 20 7842 9462;\par \par \uc2 siva.sithraputhran@dowjones.com. [ 18-03-11 1134GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020110318e73i00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
