\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 961 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 10:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HELICOPTER BEGINS DROPPING WATER ON STRICKEN POWER PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the latest attempt to cool down reactors at the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant, Japan's Self Defense Force started dropping ocean water on top of the overheated units and said that power cables from an outside source would be available as early as this afternoon. (published 0117 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ CURRENT ACCOUNT BALANCE LARGEST IN 5 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan continued aggressive emergency fund provision for a fourth straight day Thursday to calm jitters about the impact of Friday's massive earthquake and subsequent nuclear power crisis, with its current account balance expanding to its largest in five years. (published 0853 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN TRADE MINISTER KAIEDA: VERY WORRIED ABOUT YEN RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's trade minister Thursday said he is "very concerned" about the soaring yen, suggesting a heightening sense of urgency within the government of Prime Minister Naoto Kan. (published 0714 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LIFTS KEY RATES BY 25BPS; RAISES INFLATION ESTIMATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised its two key interest rates by a quarter-percentage point each Thursday, continuing its measured tightening as the fight against inflation trumps concerns of a global slowdown in growth after the Japan earthquake. (published 0841 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA ADVISER: NO RATE HIKES WARRANTED IF INFLATION EASES TO 6% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may pause its tightening moves if the inflation rate eases to 6%, C. Rangarajan, chairman of the prime minister's Economic Advisory Council said Thursday. (published 0723 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SWISS GOVT LIFTS 2011 GDP GROWTH, INFLATION FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss government Thursday raised its forecasts for economic growth and inflation this year, though the ongoing strength of the franc and the threat of a Japanese nuclear catastrophe could undermine exports and the economic recovery. (published 0804 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN WARNS ON YEN'S RECORD SURGE; G-7 READIES TELECONFERENCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen's spike to a record high against the dollar Thursday prompted warnings from Japanese officials, who blamed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength on speculation in an apparent attempt to justify potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0617 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CPI RISE COULD PEAK IN APRIL AT 5.5% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rise in China's consumer price index could hit a peak for the year of 5.5% in April but then fall to around 4% by the end of the year, Caixin media group reported Thursday on its website, citing an unnamed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official. (published 0740 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK FSA TURNER: DON'T WANT BANKS TO DISSIPATE CAPITAL THROUGH DIVIDENDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Many U.K. banks have high levels of capital, and will be encouraged not to "dissipate" it through dividends or other payments, the chief financial regulator said Thursday. (published 0816 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HK DECEMBER-FEBRUARY UNEMPLOYMENT RATE 3.6%; EXPECTED 3.8% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's unemployment rate fell to 3.6% in the three-month period ended Feb. 28 as the robust local economy continued to support the labor market, the Census and Statistics Department said Thursday. (published 0845 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MINISTER: COUNTRY'S INSURERS NOT SELLING OVERSEAS ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Economy Minister Kaoru Yosano said Thursday that market speculation about large-scale repatriation of funds by Japanese insurers is "totally groundless." (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER NODA: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOVES ARE NERVOUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Thursday he is closely watching \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, saying there have been nervous moves in thin trading conditions. (published 0109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA NDRC OFFICIAL: ACTUAL GDP GROWTH LIKELY ABOVE 7% TARGET NEXT 5 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic growth rate in the current five-year plan period, which runs from 2011 to 2015, will likely be above the government's target of 7% average annual growth, an official with the National Development and Reform Commission said Thursday. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL: YUAN APPRECIATION EXPECTATIONS OF 3% PER YEAR 'ACCEPTABLE' -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Expectations for yuan appreciation have weakened, and current expectations for appreciation of around 3% per year are in line with what China can accept, Li Bo, an official at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's department of monetary policy, was quoted as saying by Caijing magazine late Wednesday. (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  BOJ FEB. MINUTES SHOW THE CALM BEFORE THE STORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan policy board members said at the board's Feb. 14-15 meeting that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would continue to support the economy by "pursuing powerful monetary easing," meeting minutes show -- a pledge that came true a month later when a massive earthquake pushed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to move aggressively. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: JPY STRENGTH TO RETURN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: Continues to consolidate between 1.3855 and 1.4013, but downside risk is considered limited at this stage. Resistance at 1.3969 is likely to face renewed bull pressure, and a break through there would re-open Tuesday's high at 1.4013. The key Mar. 7 reaction high at 1.4036 would then come within striking distance. Loss of 1.3866 and 1.3855 would prompt a deeper corrective setback towards the Mar. 11 reaction low at 1.3752. (published 0734 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: BONDS HAVE MORE UPSIDE ROOM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: Wednesday's bullish outside day defines the short-term tone, and scope for more gains towards 124.70 has been created. A small upside gap between 122.63 and 122.66 remains unfilled, and a push through Wednesday's high at 123.92 is expected to extend the bull wave into fresh two-month highs towards 124.25 and a 1.618 Fibonacci extension target at 124.70. Corrective weakness is limited to the 122.96 area, protecting the 122.63/66 upside gap. (published 0808 GMT) [ 17-03-11 0908GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110317e73h000rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict