\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For March 14\b0\par\par\uc2 2,991 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 08:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ TAKES ADDITIONAL EASING ACTION AFTER QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan decided Monday to loosen monetary policy further by expanding an asset-buying program it introduced in October, underscoring its concerns about the economic and financial impact of the earthquake and tsunami that hit the country Friday. (published 0613 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S: JAPAN QUAKE MAY HAVE SHIFTED POTENTIAL TIPPING POINT 'A BIT FORWARD' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's massive earthquake doesn't mean that a fiscal crisis is imminent, but it may have brought the country closer to a "tipping point" where investors lose confidence in the government's finances and demand a risk premium on its bonds, a senior analyst at Moody's Investors Service said Monday. (published 0635 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STANDARD & POOR'S: QUAKE HAS NO IMMEDIATE EFFECT ON JAPAN'S CURRENT AA- RATING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The devastating earthquake that struck Japan on Friday has had a significant fiscal and economic impact on the nation's economy but has no immediate effect on its current AA- sovereign credit rating, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  debt rating agency said Monday. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPANESE FINANCE MINISTER NODA: WILL CLOSELY WATCH \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Monday he will keep a close watch on the yen's exchange rate even though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has stabilized after a spike earlier in the day. (published 0652 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: EXPLOSION AT DAIICHI NO. 3 FUKUSHIMA PLANT; 6 INJURED, 500 EVACUATED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An explosion hit the No. 3 nuclear reactor building at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Daiichi plant in Fukushima Prefecture Monday around 0201 GMT. Six people were injured and 500 were evacuated from the surrounding area. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ OFFERS TO INJECT ANOTHER Y3 TLN SAME-DAY FUNDS INTO MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan Monday offered to inject another Y3 trillion of same-day funds into the short-term money market, following its announcement in the morning it would inject a record Y12 trillion. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ OFFERS TO INJECT RECORD Y7 TRILLION SAME-DAY FUNDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan Monday offered to inject a record Y7 trillion of same-day funds into the short-term money market, aiming to secure market confidence after the massive earthquake and tsunami that struck the nation last Friday. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN YOSANO: CONVINCED MARKETS WILL CALM DOWN AS JAPAN FUNDAMENTALS FIRM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yosano also said he sees no need to change the government's view on the Japanese economy, saying the fundamentals of the economy are still healthy. (published 0202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ NOT CONDUCTING 'RATE CHECKS' IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET TODAY - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DEALER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan hasn't been conducting "rate checks" in the Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Monday, dealers said, indicating the authorities aren't preparing imminent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the strong yen. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NPC: PREMIER WEN: CONFIDENT OF MANAGING INFLATION EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said Monday that China is confident of successfully managing inflation expectations, and will continue with gradual reform of the yuan's exchange rate. (published 0543 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: CHINA PREMIER SAYS TO EXPAND FLEXIBILITY OF YUAN EXCHANGE RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao Monday said the government will continue to expand the flexibility of the yuan's exchange rate, but said any change needs to be measured because of its potentially broad economic impact. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA NPC: CHINA PREMIER WEN: LOWER GROWTH TARGET SHOWS DETERMINATION TO RESTRUCTURE ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said Monday the country's lower economic growth target for the next five years shows Beijing's determination in changing the economy's structure but cautioned the government also needs to seek a balance between maintaining growth and combating inflation. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA FEBRUARY LENDING SLOWS IN SIGN TIGHTENING MEASURES ARE WORKING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banks in China reined in new lending in February, while money supply growth slowed, a clear sign the government's monetary tightening efforts are working and further measures to cool the economy may not be necessary for now, economists said. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S ECONOMY FACES RISK OF VOLATILITY IF INFLATION RATE REMAINS HIGH - S&P \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economy faces the risk of significant volatility if the inflation rate remains high, as inflation concerns could lead to a policy over-reaction, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services said in a note Monday. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA JANUARY-FEBRUARY FISCAL REVENUE CNY1.849 TLN; UP 36% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's fiscal revenue in January and February totalled CNY1.849 trillion, up 36% from a year earlier, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA FEBRUARY WHOLESALE PRICE INDEX UP 8.31% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's inflation accelerated slightly to 8.31% in February from 8.23% in the previous month, the government said Monday. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVERNMENT: JAPAN QUAKE'S NEGATIVE IMPACT ON KOREA ECONOMY LIMITED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government said Monday it expects Japan's massive earthquake to have a limited impact on the local economy for the time being, but prolonged disruptions in logistics and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at major Japanese firms could hurt Korea's procurement of key components and eventually be detrimental to its exports. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA MINISTER: LIKELY TO DELAY RATIONING OF SUBSIDIZED FUEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesia government will likely postpone rationing of subsidized fuel on concerns it may stoke inflation further, its chief economics minister said Monday. (published 0622 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : NO EXPLICIT SIGN OF RISK AVERSION AFTER JAPAN'S QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  sees no explicit sign of risk aversion in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market after Japan's earthquake and tsunami, Assistant Governor Pongpen Ruengvirayudh said Monday. (published 0536 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : THAI FINANCIAL INSTITUTIONS UNAFFECTED BY JAPAN QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai financial institutions are unlikely to be affected by the earthquake and tsunami in Japan because they have a limited exposure to the island nation, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  Deputy Gov. Krirk Vanikkul said Monday. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : WORRIED ABOUT POSSIBLE IMPACT ON FDI FROM JAPAN QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that it's worried about the possible impact on foreign direct investment from Japan following the earthquake and tsunami disaster there. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI COMPANIES URGED TO INVEST IN JAPAN AFTER QUAKE, TSUNAMI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japan External Trade Organization on Monday urged Thai companies to invest in Japan as the north Asian country continued to battle through the aftermath of last week's earthquake and tsunami. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO FACTOR JAPAN QUAKE IN POLICY DECISION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is closely watching the impact of Friday's earthquake in Japan on global trade and commodity prices, noting that any such fallout will have a bearing on its policy decision later this month as well as the country's external payments position. (published 0208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINES AWAITS IMPACT OF JAPAN QUAKE ON SAMURAI BOND PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine government is uncertain if the earthquake that hit Japan Friday will derail the Southeast Asian nation's plan of issuing a benchmark-sized samurai bond this year to help finance its budget deficit. (published 0611 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN YOSANO: CONVINCED MARKETS WILL CALM DOWN AS JAPAN FUNDAMENTALS FIRM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Minister for Economy and Fiscal policy Kaoru Yosano on Monday played down steep falls on the Japanese stock market on the first day of trading after a massive earthquake hit the country on Friday, saying the share price falls are "within expectation." (published 0202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOYOTA MOTOR\f28 \uc2 \f2  SUSPENDS PRODUCTION AT ALL DOMESTIC PLANTS MON-WED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that it is suspending production at all domestic factories through Wednesday as the auto maker tries to adjust to the logistics dislocation wrought by Friday's massive earthquake and tsunami, as well as rolling power cuts imposed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Tepco. (published 0421 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NONLIFE INSURANCE SHARES PLUNGE ON QUAKE IMPACT CONCERN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares of nonlife insurers plunged Monday on investor concerns of the impact Japan's devastating earthquake and tsunami will have on the industry. (published 0216 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PCCW: SEVERAL SUBMARINE CABLES THAT LAND IN JAPAN HAVE BEEN AFFECTED BY QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's dominant fixed-line operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 PCCW Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that several submarine cables that land in Japan have been affected by Friday's massive earthquake, and it is switching traffic to other cable systems. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA EVERBRIGHT BANK HIRES FOUR BANKS TO HANDLE HK IPO - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Everbright Bank Co., which raised US$3.3 billion in a Shanghai initial public offering last year, has hired China Everbright Securities Ltd., \f28 \uc2 \f2 China International Capital Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  to handle its planned initial public offering in Hong Kong, people familiar with the situation said Monday. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 QBE INSURANCE\f28 \uc2 \f2  ESTIMATE US$125M OF NET CLAIMS FROM JAPAN QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 QBE Insurance Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday estimated that net claims in its business arising from an earthquake and tsunami in Japan are worth around US$125 million. (published 2303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GE'S IMMELT: WILL WORK WITH HITACHI IN JAPAN ON NUCLEAR SAFETY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 14-03-11 0714GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Electric Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jeffrey Immelt\f28 \uc2 \f2  Monday said that the company will offer technical assistance to Japanese joint venture partner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hitachi Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to avert a nuclear crisis. (published 0612 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HITACHI: PRODUCTION HALTED AT 6 FACILITIES IN QUAKE-HIT AREAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hitachi Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are currently suspended at its six manufacturing facilities in quake-struck areas. (published 0150 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MEMORY-CHIP PRICES SURGE ON ASIA SPOT MARKET FOLLOWING JAPAN EARTHQUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Memory-chip prices are surging on the spot market early Monday following the earthquake in Japan in a sign investors and companies are concerned about potential supply shortages. (published 0331 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HTC: SUPPLY CHAIN, DISTRIBUTION CHANNELS UNAFFECTED BY JAPAN QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HTC Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said a massive earthquake that struck off northeastern Japan Friday hasn't had a significant impact on its global businesses to date. (published 2354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ORIENT OVERSEAS: SHIPPING SCHEDULES TO JAPAN AFFECTED BY QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Container shipper Orient Overseas Ltd. said Monday its shipping schedules to and from Japan have been affected by Friday's massive earthquake, and the company has temporarily shut its offices in Tokyo. (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL LOGISTIC PROPERTIES CUTS JAPAN PORTFOLIO DAMAGE ESTIMATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global Logistic Properties\f28 \uc2 \f2  has reduced the estimated damage from the Japan earthquake to its Japan portfolio of properties by 18% to JPY3.17 billion . (published 2317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FAR EAST HORIZON TO START ROADSHOW WEDNESDAY FOR US$600 MLN HK IPO - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Far East Horizon Ltd., a financial-leasing unit of state-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sinochem Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , plans to launch a roadshow Wednesday for an approximately US$600 million initial public offering ahead of its listing on the Hong Kong stock exchange on March 30, a person familiar with the situation said Monday. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RIVERSDALE MINING'S RIO TINTO ACCEPTANCES AT 26.13%, UP 8.27% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shareholders in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riversdale Mining Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . backing \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s sweetened US$4.0 billion bid for the coking coal miner have risen 8.27%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday, taking the Anglo-Australian miner to 26.13% of the company's voting rights. (published 2324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA RESOURCES POWER TO BUY STAKE IN CHINESE COAL MINE FROM BANPU'S UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Power producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Resources Power Holdings Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Sunday it agreed to buy stake of a coal mine in northern China from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banpu PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Thailand's major coal miner, for $669 million. (published 2338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KDB: PRELIMINARY BIDS FOR KOREA EXPRESS DUE MARCH 25 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Monday said it and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asiana Airlines Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . have set a March 25 deadline for preliminary bids for their controlling stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Express Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0105 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PRUDENTIAL PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 : SEE MINIMAL DIRECT IMPACT ON FIRM FROM JAPAN QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prudential PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it sees limited direct impact on the company from the earthquake in Japan. (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: TECH MAHINDRA EXECUTIVE: EXPECT PRESSURE ON EUROPE CLIENTS' IT SPENDS TO EASE BY 2011-END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tech Mahindra Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects the continuing pressure on the technology spending of its clients in Europe to ease by the end of 2011, helping to strengthen revenue growth from its largest market next fiscal year. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TSMC, UMC SEE NO NEAR-TERM IMPACT ON RAW WAFER SUPPLY FROM QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwanese contract chip makers \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Microelectronics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday the earthquake in Japan on Friday won't have an effect on their raw wafer supplies in the near term as they have adequate inventories and multiple suppliers. (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ACER, ASUSTEK SEE LIMITED IMPACT FROM JAPAN QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwanese personal computer makers \f28 \uc2 \f2 Acer Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asustek Computer Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday the massive earthquake that struck off northeastern Japan on Friday hasn't had a significant impact on their global businesses. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2 : MONITORING JAPAN SITUATION, WORKING TO SECURE SUPPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's largest maker of computer memory chips and liquid crystal display panels by revenue, Monday said it will continue monitoring the situation in Japan following the devastating earthquake last week. (published 0252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SSANGYONG MOTOR GRADUATES FROM COURT-LED BANKRUPTCY PROTECTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ssangyong Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has graduated from court-led bankruptcy protection as its financial status has returned to normal after being acquired by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . last year. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RELIANCE CAPITAL: TO SELL 26% IN LIFE INSURANCE UNIT TO NIPPON LIFE FOR $680 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reliance Capital Ltd. said Monday it has agreed to sell a 26% stake in its life insurance unit to Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nippon Life Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for INR30.62 billion . (published 0554 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CENTRAL PLAZA HOTEL: 2011 NET PROFIT LIKELY CLOSE TO THB500 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Central Plaza Hotel PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a Thai hotel and restaurant operator, expects to swing to a net profit of around THB500 million this year thanks to a growing food business and the opening of new hotels. (published 0607 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HANA FINANCIAL TO PAY ADDITIONAL KRW88.84 BLN FOR 51% KEB STAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Exchange Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Monday declared a final 2010 dividend of KRW580 per share, which will require \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hana Financial Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to pay an additional KRW88.84 billion for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lone Star Funds\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' 51% stake in KEB. (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BYD CO: SEE 2011 CAR SALES GROWTH IN LINE WITH OVERALL CHINA SALES GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese battery and car maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 BYD Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it expects its 2011 car sales to grow at the same pace as sales in China's overall auto market, amid increasing competition and the cancellation of government incentives for auto purchases. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN PROPERTY DEVELOPMENT TARGETS HIGHER 2011 NET PROFIT, REVENUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian Property Development PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects net profit this year to be stronger than last year's level as revenue grows due to income from its project backlog. (published 0602 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA TELECOM NETWORKS NOT HIT BY JAPAN QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's three largest telecommunications companies--\f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Telekomunikasi Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Indosat\f28 \uc2 \f2  and PT \f28 \uc2 \f2 XL Axiata\f28 \uc2 \f2  --said Monday their networks were not affected by the massive earthquake that hit Japan on Friday. (published 0405 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KRUNG THAI BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2 : LENDING RISING; MAINTAIN 7%-8% GROWTH TARGET FOR 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Krung Thai Bank PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  is maintaining its 2011 lending growth target of at least 7%-8% despite having secured sizable loans to large corporate firms so far this year, President Apisak Tantivorawong said Monday. (published 0446 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PUBLIC BANK EXEC: WILL MAINTAIN AROUND 50% DIVIDEND PAYOUT IN MEDIUM TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Public Bank Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Malaysia's third largest lender by assets, expects to maintain its dividend payout ratio at about 50% in the medium term, Chief Operating Officer Leong Kwok Nyem said Monday. (published 0445 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: TOKYO SHARES FALL 6.1% AFTER QUAKE BUT REACTION MUTED IN OTHER MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo shares slumped 6.1% Monday after the massive quake that struck Japan and caused a destructive tsunami Friday, but bourses elsewhere in the region were only slightly lower and the Japanese yen fell, an sign that global markets were reacting fairly calmly. (published 0515 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN EDANO: POWER SUPPLY HASN'T STOPPED YET, BUT WILL STOP SOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's chief government spokesman said Monday that electric power supply hasn't stopped yet in Tokyo and the surrounding region, but that it will be inevitable to implement planned power outages within hours. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN BUSINESS REACTS TO JAPAN EARTHQUAKE ECONOMIC BLOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business and finance companies on Monday digested the impact of a devastating earthquake and tsunami that last week hit Japan, the Pacific nation's second-biggest trading partner. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: VIETNAM UNLIKELY TO RECONSIDER NUCLEAR PLANS DESPITE JAPAN PROBLEMS - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam is unlikely to reconsider its nuclear power development plans following the earthquake and tsunami-triggered problems at nuclear power plants in Japan, an official said Monday. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN RUBBER TRADE HIT AS TOCOM COMES TO A HALT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The natural rubber business in Asia was hit Monday as trading in ribbed smoked sheet 3-grade on the Tokyo Commodity Exchange came to a standstill after prices crashed through a series of circuit breaker triggers in anticipation of demand disruption due to the extensive damage caused by the earthquake that hit northeastern Japan last week. (published 0612 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA MINISTER: LNG EXPORTS TO JAPAN WON'T BE AFFECTED BY QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's exports of liquefied natural gas to Japan won't be affected by the earthquake that devastated northeastern Japan Friday, Energy & Mineral Resources Darwin Zahedy Saleh told reporters Monday. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA NPC: CHINA TO KEEP GRAIN PRICES BASICALLY STABLE -MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is able to keep grain prices basically stable, Agriculture Minister Han Changfu said Monday. (published 0149 GMT) [ 14-03-11 0714GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110314e73e000ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
